(4117579, 588312, 67697, '<td valign="top">duh woman, don''t ya know that the problem with this pic is that she is not nakkie? hehe<br/> <br/>Love the green icelandic glow here, almost spiritual.  I did not know you could get that in Toronto.<br/> <br/>Well you know that I love the pic.  It''s beautiful and certainly did not deserve the score that it got.  It should have scored higher than mine!<br/> <br/>Listen to <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">posthumous</a> and keep making beautiful photos!</td>', 'duh woman, don''t ya know that the problem with this pic is that she is not nakkie? hehe Love the green icelandic glow here, almost spiritual.  I did not know you could get that in Toronto. Well you know that I love the pic.  It''s beautiful and certainly did not deserve the score that it got.  It should have scored higher than mine! Listen to  posthumous and keep making beautiful photos!', '2007-09-26 14:00:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4117581, 588213, 66952, '<td valign="top">Also responding to your post mortem...On my work monitor, which is actually a little bright, 1/2 of the screen is pretty much totally black, except for a couple of blobs in the lower left. <br/> <br/>Another issue is the sky. Where the sun is is completely blown out, and the rest of the sky has a lot of posterization. Posterization is usually caused by going too far with the curves. Or, now that I''m looking at your editing steps, posterization can be caused by using the brightness and contrast tools. Don''t use brightness/contrast. Curves and levels can be used to adjust brightness and contrast, and are much less destructive to the image.<br/> <br/>Your reedit is much better. The people become the subject in the reedit. In this one, the sun is the subject.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Also responding to your post mortem...On my work monitor, which is actually a little bright, 1/2 of the screen is pretty much totally black, except for a couple of blobs in the lower left.  Another issue is the sky. Where the sun is is completely blown out, and the rest of the sky has a lot of posterization. Posterization is usually caused by going too far with the curves. Or, now that I''m looking at your editing steps, posterization can be caused by using the brightness and contrast tools. Don''t use brightness/contrast. Curves and levels can be used to adjust brightness and contrast, and are much less destructive to the image. Your reedit is much better. The people become the subject in the reedit. In this one, the sun is the subject. Hope this helps. ', '2007-09-26 14:01:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4117595, 588716, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ephln:</b></div><hr/><i> Love the lens effect! What lens is it? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s a 100mm macro, check the photo details for a link, etc.</td>', 'Originally posted by ephln: Love the lens effect! What lens is it?   It''s a 100mm macro, check the photo details for a link, etc.', '2007-09-26 14:04:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4117596, 588716, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roby21112:</b></div><hr/><i> I gave this a 9 thought it was a shriveled testacle. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I hope you weren''t too disappointed...</td>', 'Originally posted by roby21112: I gave this a 9 thought it was a shriveled testacle.   I hope you weren''t too disappointed...', '2007-09-26 14:05:19.000000', NULL, 0),
