(4120335, 587430, 26733, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon and the first for the 40D! This a great capture of the pier at sunset. I like going to HB pier also. Maybe I''ll see you there sometime. I''m the gray-haired lady with the 40D. (For the next few months I''ll be on crutches -- that should make it easier to spot me.)<br/>Roxanne</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon and the first for the 40D! This a great capture of the pier at sunset. I like going to HB pier also. Maybe I''ll see you there sometime. I''m the gray-haired lady with the 40D. (For the next few months I''ll be on crutches -- that should make it easier to spot me.)Roxanne', '2007-09-27 14:52:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120469, 587338, 62318, '<td valign="top">I really like the moment of the sun coming out/into the building. And the nice gold reflection on the right adds much needed depth. Gorgeous shot.</td>', 'I really like the moment of the sun coming out/into the building. And the nice gold reflection on the right adds much needed depth. Gorgeous shot.', '2007-09-27 15:53:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120471, 588511, 60173, '<td valign="top">As others have pointed out, this is a nice idea. The focus is pretty good. <br/> <br/>The composition is probably what hurt you. The image is tilted and the contrast in the window between the black and whites make it very obvious. Also the image as a whole seems off balance. I attribute this to the window framing. Your eye is naturally drawn to the whites, and they take your eye off to the left which distracts from your subject. If you were to pull back a little and frame your subject with your window, I think your photo would have a more centered direction.</td>', 'As others have pointed out, this is a nice idea. The focus is pretty good.  The composition is probably what hurt you. The image is tilted and the contrast in the window between the black and whites make it very obvious. Also the image as a whole seems off balance. I attribute this to the window framing. Your eye is naturally drawn to the whites, and they take your eye off to the left which distracts from your subject. If you were to pull back a little and frame your subject with your window, I think your photo would have a more centered direction.', '2007-09-27 15:53:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120476, 588941, 62318, '<td valign="top">I always love texture studies, and this is no exception. Nice little details enhanced from the back lighting. The two tone color works well here.</td>', 'I always love texture studies, and this is no exception. Nice little details enhanced from the back lighting. The two tone color works well here.', '2007-09-27 15:54:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120477, 587583, 62318, '<td valign="top">I actually like this photo alot. The choice of the square format works well here. The clouds in the top left give a nice balance to the cockpit on the bottom right. Actually surprised this did not do better.</td>', 'I actually like this photo alot. The choice of the square format works well here. The clouds in the top left give a nice balance to the cockpit on the bottom right. Actually surprised this did not do better.', '2007-09-27 15:56:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120481, 587991, 62318, '<td valign="top">Stunning photo. You probably had a few low votes since there is still detail in the silhouette. However, I think it is a much stronger photo the way you captured it rather that making it pure black. Congrats on the wonderful score.</td>', 'Stunning photo. You probably had a few low votes since there is still detail in the silhouette. However, I think it is a much stronger photo the way you captured it rather that making it pure black. Congrats on the wonderful score.', '2007-09-27 15:57:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120489, 587977, 62318, '<td valign="top">Nice repeating pattern. I think it might be missing some other element (not sure what what would be though). I do like the fact you submitted it for the challenge. I think it works well and shows silhouettes in a non conventional manner.</td>', 'Nice repeating pattern. I think it might be missing some other element (not sure what what would be though). I do like the fact you submitted it for the challenge. I think it works well and shows silhouettes in a non conventional manner.', '2007-09-27 15:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120492, 586895, 62318, '<td valign="top">Spirals of detail. Captiviating shot. the lens flare in the lower area might have hurt you, otherwise beauty of a shot.</td>', 'Spirals of detail. Captiviating shot. the lens flare in the lower area might have hurt you, otherwise beauty of a shot.', '2007-09-27 16:00:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120497, 588545, 62318, '<td valign="top">I like the overall framing of the shot. I think if you were just a wee bit taller, putting the tree into the lake you would have really emphasized the silhouette more. Nonethesless it is a lovely sunset shot with tons of detail especially consider shoot into the sun!</td>', 'I like the overall framing of the shot. I think if you were just a wee bit taller, putting the tree into the lake you would have really emphasized the silhouette more. Nonethesless it is a lovely sunset shot with tons of detail especially consider shoot into the sun!', '2007-09-27 16:03:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4120519, 588918, 60173, '<td valign="top">I''m sure by now you''ve figured out that your title confused a lot of people, and probably hurt your score a little bit. The first thing that bothered me about this photo from the thumbnail is how close the arm is to the left side of the image. I do this a lot myself, which is probably why it was the first thing to bug me, heh. She looks cramped because of this, I think.<br/> <br/>For an image like this to do really well on this site, I think people would want to see something more interesting done with the lighting. I know, I know, it''s a silhouette, but the lighting on the background is flat. There''s no eyecandy, basically.<br/> <br/>Which leads me to something that would have instantly bumped the score. Breasts! For a couple reasons. Firstly just the natural male attraction to them means no male would give you less than a 6, heh. Secondly, your model seems chopped. Maybe if that tidbit of breast on the right wasn''t in the photo it would seem more complete.<br/> <br/>I''m at work now, so I can''t play with the cropping, but I''m curious what it would look like if you actually cropped into the arm. Perhaps started the crop on the outside of her armpit on the left of the photo.... wait! <br/> <br/>Okay, bare with me. Actually, I just tried that in MSpaint and I think I figured out what bothers me with the lighting. She''s looking to the <br/>right side of the photo, but the light is behind her. Your eye is naturally drawn to the lightest part of the photo. She''s looking to the right, the viewer is looking to the left. This creates tension. If the light were on the right, we''d follow her gaze.<br/> <br/>(And cropping that little tidbit of breast out helped with the chopped off feeling. That distraction is no longer there.)<br/> <br/>Sorry to have rambled a bit. No time to edit! I''m already 15 minutes over my lunch break, heh.<br/> <br/>Edit: I thought I''d come back and show you the crop I was talking about.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=596210" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60173/120/596210.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60173/120/596210.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60173/120/596210.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-06 16:01:21.</i></td>', 'I''m sure by now you''ve figured out that your title confused a lot of people, and probably hurt your score a little bit. The first thing that bothered me about this photo from the thumbnail is how close the arm is to the left side of the image. I do this a lot myself, which is probably why it was the first thing to bug me, heh. She looks cramped because of this, I think. For an image like this to do really well on this site, I think people would want to see something more interesting done with the lighting. I know, I know, it''s a silhouette, but the lighting on the background is flat. There''s no eyecandy, basically. Which leads me to something that would have instantly bumped the score. Breasts! For a couple reasons. Firstly just the natural male attraction to them means no male would give you less than a 6, heh. Secondly, your model seems chopped. Maybe if that tidbit of breast on the right wasn''t in the photo it would seem more complete. I''m at work now, so I can''t play with the cropping, but I''m curious what it would look like if you actually cropped into the arm. Perhaps started the crop on the outside of her armpit on the left of the photo.... wait!  Okay, bare with me. Actually, I just tried that in MSpaint and I think I figured out what bothers me with the lighting. She''s looking to the right side of the photo, but the light is behind her. Your eye is naturally drawn to the lightest part of the photo. She''s looking to the right, the viewer is looking to the left. This creates tension. If the light were on the right, we''d follow her gaze. (And cropping that little tidbit of breast out helped with the chopped off feeling. That distraction is no longer there.) Sorry to have rambled a bit. No time to edit! I''m already 15 minutes over my lunch break, heh. Edit: I thought I''d come back and show you the crop I was talking about. ', '2007-09-27 16:17:00.000000', '2007-10-06 17:01:21.000000', 0),
