(4123795, 588453, 52942, '<td valign="top">thank you everyone. haha i thought this shot would probably get last place, and i wasnt too close from being wrong. :P hahaha....but i really appreciate the comments.<br/> <br/>it wasnt so noisy until i converted it to jpeg. i suppose it really killed it :\ <br/> <br/>yeah, the trees are boring, i hadnt planned on submitting anything but i happened to take a picture with SOMETHING silhoutted, so...haha. i never noticed how blurry it really is...it always looks better in the imaging programm and on the camera...<br/> <br/>the colors i had to pump up (it looked more beautiful and brilliant in the sky believe it or not, but it captured it looking real grey and dull when the sky was actually pink and purplish....)...but behind the trees theres some purple stuff i didnt want but couldnt get rid of...oh well! (and yeah, i think i did have the ISO too high, 1600 i think...eeep)<br/> <br/>thank you everyone for your time and your help, its much appreciated. hopefully one day i''ll submit something better, haha. :)</td>', 'thank you everyone. haha i thought this shot would probably get last place, and i wasnt too close from being wrong. :P hahaha....but i really appreciate the comments. it wasnt so noisy until i converted it to jpeg. i suppose it really killed it :\  yeah, the trees are boring, i hadnt planned on submitting anything but i happened to take a picture with SOMETHING silhoutted, so...haha. i never noticed how blurry it really is...it always looks better in the imaging programm and on the camera... the colors i had to pump up (it looked more beautiful and brilliant in the sky believe it or not, but it captured it looking real grey and dull when the sky was actually pink and purplish....)...but behind the trees theres some purple stuff i didnt want but couldnt get rid of...oh well! (and yeah, i think i did have the ISO too high, 1600 i think...eeep) thank you everyone for your time and your help, its much appreciated. hopefully one day i''ll submit something better, haha. :)', '2007-09-29 01:36:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4123877, 588772, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by muz64:</b></div><hr/><i> Beautiful photo. One question, though... With a shutter speed of 30sec, how come there are no star trails? Did you use a tracking mount? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I checked my original. I can see the slight star trails in my original. I think the trails became almost round due to resizing and sharpening. Ha, I wish I could buy that kind of fancy motor and telescope now.</td>', 'Originally posted by muz64: Beautiful photo. One question, though... With a shutter speed of 30sec, how come there are no star trails? Did you use a tracking mount?  I checked my original. I can see the slight star trails in my original. I think the trails became almost round due to resizing and sharpening. Ha, I wish I could buy that kind of fancy motor and telescope now.', '2007-09-29 03:06:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4124004, 587546, 42902, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by elizadeb:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by elizadeb:</b></div><hr/><i> My Gosh.... soooooooooo underrated! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I gave it a 10 (plus) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I didn''t expect to get only tens but then, I didn''t expect to get twos either :(<br/> <br/>I guess my perspective doesn''t match the one of the majority voting on this site...<br/> <br/>Thanks for the high vote though. It''s much appreciated :)</td>', 'Originally posted by elizadeb: Originally posted by elizadeb: My Gosh.... soooooooooo underrated!  I gave it a 10 (plus)   I didn''t expect to get only tens but then, I didn''t expect to get twos either :( I guess my perspective doesn''t match the one of the majority voting on this site... Thanks for the high vote though. It''s much appreciated :)', '2007-09-29 07:27:33.000000', NULL, 0),
