(4156095, 586964, 84198, '<td valign="top">Keep in mind this shot was taken from about 5 feet away.  The spider is/was about 10 feet off the ground or 3 feet above the 5-ft bushes.  I couldn''t exactly get any closer to it, not that I personally wanted to (I''m scared of spiders, yet fascinated by them).</td>', 'Keep in mind this shot was taken from about 5 feet away.  The spider is/was about 10 feet off the ground or 3 feet above the 5-ft bushes.  I couldn''t exactly get any closer to it, not that I personally wanted to (I''m scared of spiders, yet fascinated by them).', '2007-10-10 01:41:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4157833, 586878, 77287, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by man:</b></div><hr/><i> nice photo but missing silhoute </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Eh?????</td>', 'Originally posted by man: nice photo but missing silhoute   Eh?????', '2007-10-10 14:27:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4158130, 586878, 39850, '<td valign="top">Nice simple yet interesting image.  Like the colors, composition, framing and crop.  Even without the movement in the sky, still be a good image.  Make a nice ''wall sized'' piece of ''art''.  Parts of the red (sun) seems to be bordering on overcontrast/blown/something, but minor.  The coloring masks it well anyway.  Good meet of the Challenge.  I didn''t vote, but hypothetically likely would have given this an 8 or 9.</td>', 'Nice simple yet interesting image.  Like the colors, composition, framing and crop.  Even without the movement in the sky, still be a good image.  Make a nice ''wall sized'' piece of ''art''.  Parts of the red (sun) seems to be bordering on overcontrast/blown/something, but minor.  The coloring masks it well anyway.  Good meet of the Challenge.  I didn''t vote, but hypothetically likely would have given this an 8 or 9.', '2007-10-10 16:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4160535, 587273, 62318, '<td valign="top">I have yet to see that movie, but it is on my list...<br/> <br/>I like the angle of the silhouette. Maybe a bit more depth of field, but the lighting hitting the face is terrific.</td>', 'I have yet to see that movie, but it is on my list... I like the angle of the silhouette. Maybe a bit more depth of field, but the lighting hitting the face is terrific.', '2007-10-11 15:20:12.000000', NULL, 0);
